set -eu
# The other half, and the one that matters more: sleep does not suppress a stall, it is subtracted
# from one. The transcript is forty minutes old and the host slept for ten of them, so thirty
# minutes of awake inactivity remain — exactly the threshold — and the notification goes out as it
# always did.
#
# The event keeps `transcript_age_seconds` at the wall age, because that is what was observed, and
# carries `awake_age_seconds` beside it. A line that said "no transcript change for 30 m" about a
# transcript last touched forty minutes ago would have traded one wrong number for another.
"$BATON" tick
